  \approx 24V$, and a load $R_{load} \approx 3.3 \Omega$. The high-frequency    
  switching (chattering) occurs because the target thresholds are outside the   
  region where the steady-state attracts the system at the current operating    
  voltage, effectively forcing the system to oscillate between the              
  thresholds.")                                                                 
                                                                                
